{"baseRefName":"main","baseRefOid":"efd29c05204703acca9a0860812f54b94fae54b1","body":"## Disposition\nOriginal **30005116 / OWR-10252930-028 remains unsolved after 5/5 substantive author turns**. Full independent AI-assisted source/proof review passes the scoped results with no mandatory correction.\n\nThe target is the unrestricted induced-C4 profile at prescribed edge density above one half. None of the restricted classes or local topologies below is silently substituted for that target.\n\n## Reviewed results\n- Exact optimization of the proposed construction over every multipartite part count\n- Density-preserving replacement for complete joins with low-density internal blocks, and a consequence for all asymptotic triangle-minimizing sequences using the credited Pikhurko–Razborov theorem\n- Explicit non-multipartite paw blow-ups tying the construction value, with positive edit separation from multipartite graphons; these are ties, not source counterexamples\n- Strict local control for small L-infinity edge amplitudes, together with exact L1-close tying paths that prevent an edit-distance uniqueness shortcut\n- The full proposed profile for every weighted cograph and every cograph sequence, proved by coupled-density join/union induction at arbitrary cotree depth\n- The exact rank-one latent-product profile and equality cases, strictly below the achievable source construction at every interior density\n\nArbitrary non-cograph, non-rank-one hosts with positive triangle excess remain outside these arguments. Induced vertex-set density is distinguished from labeled patterns, ordinary C4 counts and finite-graph versus graphon edge normalization. The scan through order six is supplementary to the all-size cograph proof.\n\n## Frozen verification\nAll **36 author files and six review files** are unchanged. **93,505 author assertions** replay byte-for-byte; **1,080 independent exact controls** pass. The author scripts use standard-library Python; the independent symbolic checker additionally requires **SymPy**.\n\nThe additive `verify_publication.py` stages only frozen author files, passes that directory explicitly to the reviewer replay and compares both review outputs exactly. The unbound `WORKING_AUDIT.txt` is excluded.\n\n- Author checkpoint: `e27668a5dd99e38705ec6a97d15710b7eb1b0f41`\n- Author manifest: `e594f4629756fbf1a8b372d677de4f174f01f3886d3fa8c58c9dcc87c86fb2fa`\n- Review report: `2363f7563d25f1b117af72e737008731ca7ff04f69b43d3837bede8f58c7d766`\n- Review manifest: `44bfd745f1502e86301b644c6f1390ba73f72929215c84bbf1a994c6063675fe`\n- Publication manifest: `a9bdf8fb55120df14ced979cd8388b652e80c3ea822be20aae5a7c911d4502c5`\n\nThe [primary source](https://ems.press/journals/owr/articles/10252930) is OWR22/2022, printed1227–1228, published14April2023. All source constructions, prior bounds and structural inputs are credited. No historical novelty, human peer review or formal verification is claimed.\n\nFresh main `efd29c05204703acca9a0860812f54b94fae54b1` and final author ancestry are retained. Exactly45 target artifacts and the sole target QUEUE status/turn cells change. All46 raw remote paths are byte-exact. Source PDFs, screenshots, extracts, HTML, imports and private coordination are excluded.\n\nDraft only; no merge or release.","commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-10-02T17:05:17Z","authors":[{"email":"me@aleckriebel.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","login":"AlecKriebel","name":"Alec Kriebel"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-02T17:05:17Z","messageBody":"…resolved","messageHeadline":"Checkpoint induced C4 turn 1: exact multipartite profile, original un…","oid":"4b3af41c5eb68f29409ca55f5784ed6291552f38"},{"authoredDate":"2026-10-02T17:25:54Z","authors":[{"email":"me@aleckriebel.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMDkzNzA=","login":"AlecKriebel","name":"Alec Kriebel"}],"committedDate":"2026-10-02T17:25:54Z","messageBody":"…tite ties","messageHeadline":"Checkpoint induced C4 turn 2: exact join replacement and non-multipar…","oid":"f6844b255c7699